<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_games",
    "Open a game from Retro Games and press Play with someone. That creates a match room and drops you into it as its host, with one empty seat opposite you. Nothing has been sent anywhere yet."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_link}>{dgettext("help_games", "The link comes from Share")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_games",
    "Inside the room, Share mints the address, shows it, and puts a Copy button beside it. Paste it into a channel or a private message and it draws a card with the game on it and the number of seats left. Opening the game does not create an address — pressing Share does, so you never leave links behind for rooms nobody used."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_join}>{dgettext("help_games", "Ready, then Start")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_games",
    "Whoever follows the link takes the seat and lands in the same room. Both of you press Ready, and then the host's Start begins the match. There is no accept step for the game itself: the link named it, and following the link was the agreement."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lock}>{dgettext("help_games", "Who can play")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_games",
    "Creating a match link needs a registered nickname you have identified with NickServ, and so does taking the seat. Somebody either of you has blocked cannot join, and neither can you join your own match from a second window."
  )}
</p>

<p>
  {dgettext("help_games", "See also:")}
  <.help_link topic="feature-game-match-full">
    {dgettext("help_games", "Why a Match Link Stopped Working")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-retro-games">
    {dgettext("help_games", "Retro Games")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
